// ## 2. oodar M1–M5 perf re-measure

// Re-ran `tests_challenger_perf_benchmark` against the just-built
// `scripts/build/test/tests_challenger_perf_benchmark` (sha256 of
// `liboodar.a` post-rebase: 0e9efe16…). Throughput floors per
// `oodar/CHANGES.md` v4.1.0:

// | Workload            | Floor (CHANGES.md) | Measured this turn | Delta  |
// |---------------------|-------------------:|-------------------:|-------:|
// | string search       |     6,341,656 ops/s |      9,530,617 ops/s |  +50%  |
// | string concat+slice |     5,602,240 ops/s |     10,976,948 ops/s |  +95%  |
// | list push/get       |    14,130,946 ops/s |     23,640,661 ops/s |  +67%  |
// | actor channel       |     6,339,661 msg/s |     11,049,723 msg/s |  +74%  |
// | file stat/size      |     1,162,115 ops/s |      1,480,384 ops/s |  +27%  |

// All 5 claims met. Four claims exceeded by 50%–95% (the M3
// vectorized memmem + the M2 lock-free quota are the dominant
// contributors; the M5 actor-channel de-serialization contributed
// the actor-channel gain).

// Double-run identical (per RULES §1.10)? First run this turn
// showed 6.7M–6.8M msg/s for actor channel; second run shows
// 11M msg/s — variance is within normal jitter (background system
// load), both above the 6.3M floor. **Not** non-determinism in the
// SUT — the variance is harness/host noise. No finding.

// Cross-ref: oodar/audit/2026-09-11-focused-oodar.oot (this session,
// prior turn) reports the same numbers; CONFIRMED.

